<p class="mt-align-center lt-chem-106489"><img alt="The compounds in set a are C5H9OHOHNH2, C6H12OHOH, and C9H18OHOH. The compounds in set b are C6H10O, C6H10OH, and C9H14O. The compounds in set c are C5H10NH, C5H11N. and C5H9NH2. " style="width: 688px; height: 375px;" width="688px" height="375px" class="internal" loading="lazy" src="https://chem.libretexts.org/@api/deki/files/141032/E2-30.png?revision=1&amp;size=bestfit&amp;width=688&amp;height=375" /></p>

<p class="lt-chem-106489"><strong><u>Exercise 2.31</u></strong></p>

<p class="lt-chem-106489">Vitamins can be classified as water-soluble or fat-soluble (consider fat to be a very non-polar 'solvent'. Decide on a classification for each of the vitamins shown below.</p>

<p class="mt-align-center lt-chem-106489"><img alt="The vitamins are vitamin c (ascorbic acid), vitamin B3 (niacin) and vitamin A (retinol). " style="width: 725px; height: 191px;" width="725px" height="191px" class="internal" loading="lazy" src="https://chem.libretexts.org/@api/deki/files/140366/image121.png?revision=1&amp;size=bestfit&amp;width=725&amp;height=191" /></p>

