<p class="lt-chem-106489">Both aniline and phenol are mostly insoluble in pure water. Predict the solubility of these two compounds in 10% aqueous hydrochloric acid, and explain your reasoning.</p>

<p class="mt-align-center lt-chem-106489"><img alt="Bond line drawings of aniline and phenol. " style="width: 209px; height: 141px;" width="209px" height="141px" class="internal" loading="lazy" src="https://chem.libretexts.org/@api/deki/files/140360/image123.png?revision=1&amp;size=bestfit&amp;width=209&amp;height=141" /></p>

<p class="lt-chem-106489"><strong><u>Exercise 2.33</u></strong></p>

